# Applies to every `docker build` in this repo, whichever Dockerfile is
# used — Docker only reads one .dockerignore, from the build context root
# (the repo root; both apps/api/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile are
# built with `-f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .` for exactly this reason, so
# `turbo prune`'s COPY . . step inside the pruner stage — see either
# Dockerfile — sees the whole monorepo). See docs/DECISIONS.md D9.13.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.next-e2e
**/.turbo
**/coverage
.git
.cache

# Local env/secrets never belong in an image — real deployments inject
# config via the platform's env/secrets mechanism (see apps/*/Dockerfile
# and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md), not a baked-in file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor/OS cruft, docs, and CI config — none of it is needed to build
# either app, and excluding it keeps the build context (and Docker's
# hashing of it) small.
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
.github
docs

# Playwright/test artifacts that sometimes land at repo root locally.
playwright-report
test-results
